      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this is called from create and update, we might beed to be a bit more clever.  While fine for create, think of the following update scenario.\n\n1) I\u0027m using \u0027region\u0027 rather than \u0027region_id\"\n\n2) I create the endpoint with endpoint[\u0027region\u0027] \u003d my-region\n\n3) This succeeds and my-region is auto-created\n\n4) I then want to move the endpoint to my-other-region\n\n5) So I do:\n* ref \u003d get_endpoint()\n* ref[\u0027region\u0027] \u003d my-other-region\n*update_endpoint()\n\n...which will not work, since region_id is ALSO defined\n\nWhat I think we need to do is examine both region and region_id for the update case and see if either have been changed.  If they are updating using \u0027region\u0027 then we support that (and auto create if necessary)",
